## Control {{controlId}}: Cryptographic Mechanisms for Remote Access Confidentiality

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization employs cryptographic mechanisms to protect the confidentiality of remote access sessions within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Transport-layer encryption (TLS 1.2+) protects all remote access communications, while authentication methods enforce cryptographic validation through phishing-resistant credentials.

{{#if mfaEnabled}}
Multi-factor authentication is enforced with {{authMethodsCount}} configured authentication methods providing cryptographic session protection:
{{#if authMethods}}
{{#each authMethods}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Provides cryptographic authentication validation{{#if (eq id "Fido2")}} via hardware security key{{/if}}{{#if (eq id "MicrosoftAuthenticator")}} via push notification with number matching{{/if}}.
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
All remote sessions use TLS 1.2 or higher for transport encryption, with Azure AD enforcing FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic modules in the GCC High environment.
{{else}}
MFA and cryptographic authentication methods have not been configured. Remote access confidentiality relies on transport encryption only, pending MFA deployment.
{{/if}}

{{#if policies}}
Conditional Access policies enforce cryptographic protection:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{#if grantControls.authenticationStrength}} with {{grantControls.authenticationStrength}} authentication strength{{/if}}.
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

